iol</source><year>1996</year><volume>81</volume><fpage>2095</fpage><lpage>104</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8941534</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fedele</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>CV</given-names></name><name><surname>Farrell</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Selected contribution: IGF-I antibody prevents increases in protein synthesis in epitrochlearis muscles from reefed, diabetic rats</article-title><source>J App Physiol</source><year>2001</year><volume>90</volume><fpage>1166</fpage><lpage>1173</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holecek</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sprongl</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Tilser</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Metabolism of branched-chain amino acids in starved rats: the role of hepatic tissue</article-title><source>Physiol Res</source><year>2001</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>25</fpage><lpage>33</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11300224</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Proud</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Regulation of mammalian translation factors by nutrients</article-title><source>Euro J Biochem</source><year>2002</year><volume>269</volume><fpage>5338</fpage><lpage>5349</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1432-1033.2002.03292.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nishitani</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Matsumura</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Fujitani</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sonaka</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Miura</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Yagasaki</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Leucine promotes glucose uptake in skeletal muscles of rats</article-title><source>Biochem Bioph Res Com</source><year>2002</year><volume>299</volume><fpage>693</fpage><lpage>696</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0006-291X(02)02717-1</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Freinkel</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Metzger</surname><given-names>BE</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Wilson JD, Foster DW</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Metabolic changes in pregnancy</article-title><source>Williams Textbook of Endocrinology</source><year>1992</year><edition>8</edition><publisher-name>Saunders, Philadelphia</publisher-name><fpage>993</fpage><lpage>1006</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gomes-Marcondes</surname><given-names>MCC</given-names></name><name><surname>Cury</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Curi</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Consequences of Walker 256 tumor growth for the placental/fetal development in rats</article-title><source>Cancer Res Ther Contr</source><year>1998</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>277</fpage><lpage>283</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ventrucci</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Mello</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Gomes-Marcondes</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><